line-protocol-parser (2.0.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Align the single-line parser more closely with archived InfluxDB
    v1.2 behavior while keeping Python comment-line convenience.
  * Return None when timestamps are omitted instead of conflating
    omission with an explicit 0 timestamp.
  * Reject malformed keys, values, duplicate tags, trailing junk,
    oversized measurement/tag keys, and other invalid input that older
    releases accepted.
  * Update the C API point model to use has_time plus signed time and
    add the max-key-length status code.
  * Require Python 3.10 or newer.

 -- Daniel Andersson <daniel.4ndersson@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Mar 2026 13:30:00 +0100

